{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>For a shame among their rivals.</b> Rashi and all the commentators explain it from the language of bringing out an evil report, from the language of the Sages: ״שמץ פסול״ — a suspicion of disqualification. And Moses says that Aaron was the cause that the coming generations would bring out an evil report against Israel, saying that all of them had their intent directed toward idolatry, so that through this the evil report would spread among their rivals and become for them a reproach and a byword among the nations." "<b>And the correct interpretation</b> is what the Ramban, of blessed memory, explained: that the word לשמצה is from the language of diminution, as in (Job 4:12) ״ותקח אזני שמץ מנהו״, and it is written (Job 26:14) ״ומה שמץ דבר נשמע בו״. And Moses says that there was cause in this, in order to weaken their merit and diminish them before the enemies when they go out to war, in the manner of what is written (Ezekiel 29:15) ״והמעטתים לבלתי רדות בגוים״, and it is written (Jeremiah 10:24) ״יסרני ה׳ אך במשפט אל באפך פן תמעיטני״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:06:33.093414083Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}